unity of north america  where all the economies are growing  um actually help solve that problem too  so i think  you know leadership from the united  states to drive growth  will help solve some of these other  issues too you've also seen nafta  from both sides of the border you've  seen that issue which is another hot  issue right now in the united states has  nafta overall been good or bad for the  united states  my view would be that free trade deals  are good overall for  all participants and i think it's been  good for north america and  all the countries all the countries in  it doesn't mean it's perfect  very few free trade deals are perfect so  can it be made better  yes i hope they can make it better but i  don't think we should  start uh uh deconstructing global trade  i think it's been a powerful engine uh  for lifting all boats  it doesn't mean it solved all problems  there are questions of income inequality  there are questions of not all the rules  were were perfect and need to be  improved  but let's go forward not backwards so  when president trump trump first came in  he was very closely allied with  many people in business he consulted he  had panels that he talked with as well  do you get to talk either president  trump or the administration about things  like nafta i mean do they consult you or  do you  make your views known to them when there  are things where we have a  view or it affects our business we make  our views known  either directly to the administration or  through many of the the business forums  like the business roundtable uh there  are there are enough points of  intersection  um collectively and individually with  the administration that  everyone they know what uh they know  what we think so from that do you have  any sense of where we're headed with  nafta because there's the conflicting  reports i mean the canadians  seem to be preparing for actually u.s  withdrawal there are a lot of people in  washington say no we're not g