n your  app no but you have to get it  i mean you know if you went back even  two or three years in china for example  uh when a lot of the apps and the and  the and the the mobile payment systems  came in  uh we weren't on the menu actually even  worse we were trying to sell perhaps a  returnable glass bottle to the  restaurant  which had no way of being in the  delivery system so we've had to  re-engineer our business system very  quickly to both  be present on the app so what's the  virtual representation of what you'd  normally see in the store  and how do we change the packaging  portfolio so that we can be part of the  delivery system and you have a lot of  places in shanghai  where all food ordered on apps and  delivered is thirty fifty percent of  the of the restaurant sales that's  relationship with the consumer  talk about coca-cola as coca-cola how is  technology changing the way you do  business and for that matter your  workforce  it's changing it in lots of profound  ways i mean in in simple terms  you know you go back 10 20 years we were  a large company and we're one of the few  that could afford to invest  in expensive it systems and do our own  stuff our own programs our own server  farms  you wind forward to today that's no  longer the model we've had to move to  the cloud  we've had to move to standard uh  programs that whole industries use and  we had to use the mobile  um the one thing i always say to the it  department is  just put it on the phone everything can  be done on the phone let's just move  everything to mobile on the phone the  the old days of it had training budgets  why everyone knows how to use the apps  on the phone so it's profoundly changing  the way the way that we work and i think  it's going to continue  to flow through the organization we have  a big program of digitizing the company  does that translate into fewer employees  as a practical matter because of the  efficiencies from digital  i think it for sure it changes in